UID:dbc85beab83a@paris-academique
DTSTAMP:20260611T125335Z
DTSTART:20260611T103000
DTEND:20260611T120000
SUMMARY:Alexis Marchand\, "Stable commutator length\, spectral gaps\, and negative curvature in groups"
DESCRIPTION:Stable commutator length (scl) is a measure of homological complexity of group elements\, with connections to many topics in group theory and geometric topology\, including quasimorphisms\, bounded cohomology\, and circle actions. The first part of the talk will be a general introduction to scl and to some of these topics In the second part\, we will focus on spectral gaps and their relation with notio\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16149/
LOCATION:IHP\, 11 rue Pierre et Marie Curie\, Paris 5e
URL:https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16149/
END:VEVENT
