DTSTART:20260612T103000
DTEND:20260612T113000
SUMMARY:Boundary contacts for reflected random walks in the quarter plane
DESCRIPTION:Reflected random walks in the quarter plane arise naturally in probability theory\, queueing systems\, statistical physics\, and combinatorics. In this talk\, I will discuss the local time spent on the reflection boundaries. When the drift lies within the cone\, the local time converges\, without normalization\, to a nontrivial random variable as the walk length tends to infinity. I will present recent r\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16405/
LOCATION:Tours
URL:https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16405/
END:VEVENT
